{"id": 22, "ts": 1780458647.5527966, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "emily_brooks", "message": "I appreciate the clarification on Candidate\u202fC\u2019s stress resilience \u2013 \u201ckeeps calm in a crisis\u201d shows he can maintain performance under pressure, matching Candidate\u202fB\u2019s strength in that area. Combined with C\u2019s 100\u202f% reliability, rapid correct decision\u2011making, and a positive crew atmosphere, his profile now looks considerably stronger than we initially thought.\nHowever, the remaining concerns for C \u2013 difficulty communicating ideas, an egocentric demeanor, and a lack of willingness to pursue further education \u2013 still raise serious questions about crew\u2011resource\u2011management and adaptability on long\u2011haul flights. Candidate\u202fB, while occasionally pretentious and occasionally using the wrong tone, demonstrates solid technical competence (weather assessment, computer skills) and a proven conscientious work ethic, which are critical for the operational demands of international routes.\nGiven that B\u2019s technical and analytical strengths remain unmatched, and his communication issues appear more manageable through training, I will keep my provisional vote for Candidate\u202fB, while recognizing Candidate\u202fC as the strongest alternative that warrants further probing on technical competence and adaptability."}
