{"id": 26, "ts": 1780458700.419865, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "sarah_mitchell", "message": "I agree with Emily and James that Candidate\u202fB remains our strongest overall fit.\u202fWhile Candidate\u202fC is 100\u202f% reliable, makes quick correct decisions, and keeps calm in a crisis, his difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric demeanor, and lack of willingness to pursue further education raise serious concerns for crew\u2011resource\u2011management and adaptability on long\u2011haul flights.\u202fCandidate\u202fD, despite excellent problem\u2011solving and responsibility, is reported as arrogant with weak leadership, which could undermine cockpit teamwork.\u202fCandidate\u202fA\u2019s unorganized nature and poor response to criticism also threaten operational reliability and crew cooperation.\u202fIn contrast, Candidate\u202fB\u2019s very conscientious work ethic, proven stress resilience, strong weather\u2011assessment ability, and excellent computer skills directly support the reliability, technical competence, and attention\u2011to\u2011detail required for international routes.\u202fAlthough B\u2019s pretentious tone and occasional grumpiness are noted, these communication quirks appear more manageable through CRM training than the deeper interpersonal issues seen in the other candidates.\u202fTherefore, I maintain my provisional vote for Candidate\u202fB."}
